    "summary": "Stellar Truckin' > Weather Report Suite jam & tight second‑set flow",
    "blurb": "The show shines with a monster Truckin' → Weather Report Suite Prelude → Wharf Rat sequence, plus fiery versions of Here Comes Sunshine and Candyman. Jerry’s tone is clean and soaring, Phil lays down powerful bass lines, and Bill’s single‑drummer groove drives the high‑energy second set.",
    "review": "On March 26 1973 at the Baltimore Civic Center the Dead delivered a performance that still feels fresh. The first set rolls through tour staples with solid playing, but it’s the second set that truly lifts off – a seamless, high‑octane suite that begins with a ripping Truckin' into the Weather Report Suite Prelude and explodes into an unforgettable Wharf Rat climax. Jerry Garcia’s guitar is “cooking” all night; his soaring solos on Here Comes Sunshine, Truckin' and Candyman are highlighted by a clean, passionate tone that deadheads rave about. Phil Lesh provides powerful ending notes on Morning Dew, hits high‑notes in Eyes Of The World, and adds a sweet groove to China Cat Sunflower. Keith Godchaux is “on big time,” supplying strong backing chords and tasteful fills that lift the jams, while Bill Kreutzmann’s tight single‑drummer groove anchors the relentless momentum. The crystal‑clear Miller soundboard transfer captures every nuance, making this one of the most compelling 1973 shows available.",
